From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:48:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] MCP for agents: drafts, on-demand sync, attachments;
 fork image and checks

- crates/server/src/mcp: MCP endpoint at /mcp (BICHON_ENABLE_MCP), based on
  upstream's unfinished feature/add-mcp branch. Tools: list_accounts,
  list_folders, sync_now, search_emails, get_email, get_thread,
  save_attachments, save_draft. Nothing sends, deletes or moves mail.
- save_draft builds the message (reply threading, attachments from
  BICHON_MCP_FILES_DIR only) and APPENDs it to \Drafts with \Draft \Seen.
- Account permissions account:sync and data:draft for agent tokens.
- Single JSON-RPC responses instead of one-element batches (MCP 2025-06-18).
- docker/svesh.Dockerfile (from source, uid 1000), svesh-build workflow
  (check -> image to ghcr.io/svesh87/bichon), Renovate for the fork's own
  build and upstream releases, SVESH.md.
- Checks: rustfmt, clippy, MCP tests incl. a scripted IMAP server, line
  coverage of the MCP module >= 80% (94.6% now).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
